      "message": "Left a TODO.\n\nNote that cross-compiling C++ and Go at the same time might prove tricky. For example, this invocation fails (using an arbitrary Go target):\n\n```\n$ bazel build //infra/bots/task_drivers/bazel_build --config\u003dlinux_rbe --platforms\u003d//bazel/platform:pixel_5,@io_bazel_rules_go//go/toolchain:linux_amd64\n...\nERROR: \n.../skia/infra/bots/task_drivers/bazel_build/BUILD.bazel:19:10: GoLink infra/bots/task_drivers/bazel_build/bazel_build_/bazel_build failed: (Exit 1): builder failed: error executing command bazel-out/k8-opt-exec-81C6BA4F/bin/external/go_sdk_linux_amd64/builder \u0027-param\u003dbazel-out/k8-fastbuild/bin/infra/bots/task_drivers/bazel_build/bazel_build_/bazel_build-0.params\u0027 -- -linkmode internal ... (remaining 1 argument skipped)\nruntime.gcdata: missing Go type information for global symbol .dynsym: size 24\nlink: error running subcommand external/go_sdk_linux_amd64/pkg/tool/linux_amd64/link: exit status 2\nTarget //infra/bots/task_drivers/bazel_build:bazel_build failed to build\n```\n\nIf we depend on a Go program to run an Android test, I anticipate we\u0027ll run into similar issues. I need to investigate what\u0027s going on in the above error.",
